-- dispatch: derivation over the three structural shapes (§9.2, §9.3) and
-- the `parts` contract of §9 — one `Target` per structural position, fields
-- sorted by name TEXT and tuple elements 0…n−1.
--
-- A shape key is the field-name list or the arity, never the field TYPES
-- (A.11): `{ x : Int, y : Int }` and `{ x : Int, y : String }` share one
-- `r$x$y` function and differ only in the evidence they are given, which is
-- what bounds the emitted-function count by shapes instead of
-- instantiations. Both records below are that one entry.
--
-- The declarations are in the REVERSE of the order the derived functions
-- sort in, so the sort is load-bearing: request order is `unit`, `t2`,
-- `r$x$y`, and §8.5's order — by printed name text — is the other way
-- round. A table that printed request order would pass with the wrong
-- numbering and `derived 0` would name a different function than the
-- emitter's first (A.15, A.29).
pub sameUnit : (), () → Bool
sameUnit a b = a == b


pub samePair : Int × Char, Int × Char → Bool
samePair a b = a == b


pub sameInts : { x : Int, y : Int }, { x : Int, y : Int } → Bool
sameInts a b = a == b


pub sameMixed : { y : String, x : Int }, { y : String, x : Int } → Bool
sameMixed a b = a == b
